SUGGESTED FIXES - UltraFast methodology guidance
------------------------------------------------
Examples are illustrative; adapt names and preserve interface behavior.

UF006 | Unregistered module output
------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Suggested change: For a timing-sensitive boundary, move output combinational logic before an
  existing output register or add an output register. Keep a deliberate combinational adapter
  unchanged when latency must remain zero, and document that decision with a targeted waiver.
Check before accepting: Align data, valid and sideband signals. For ready/valid or AXI interfaces
  use a protocol-correct register slice or skid-buffer design; never delay ready/valid
  independently. Check latency in simulation.
UltraFast basis: UG949 recommends registering outputs at logical boundaries to keep timing paths
  local and easier to analyze.
AMD UG949: https://docs.amd.com/r/en-US/ug949-vivado-design-methodology/Register-Data-Paths-at-Logical-Boundaries
Illustrative VHDL:
    -- Example for a simple synchronous datapath, not an AXI slice.
    process(clk)
    begin
      if rising_edge(clk) then
        result_q <= result_comb;
      end if;
    end process;
    result_out <= result_q;
Illustrative Verilog / SystemVerilog:
    // Simple datapath example; not an AXI register slice.
    always @(posedge clk) result_q <= result_comb;
    assign result_out = result_q;

UF007 | Raw input used before capture
------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Suggested change: If the interface permits an added cycle, capture the synchronous input into a
  local register and route its internal consumers through that register. Remove unintended raw-input
  bypasses. A combinational pass-through or monitor may intentionally remain unregistered.
Check before accepting: A single input register is not a CDC solution. Preserve handshake and
  sideband alignment; confirm latency and stall behavior before changing the boundary.
UltraFast basis: UG949 suggests considering registered inputs as well as outputs at hierarchical
  boundaries.
AMD UG949: https://docs.amd.com/r/en-US/ug949-vivado-design-methodology/Register-Data-Paths-at-Logical-Boundaries
Illustrative VHDL:
    -- Example for a same-clock data input with one-cycle latency.
    process(clk)
    begin
      if rising_edge(clk) then
        input_q <= input_data;
      end if;
    end process;
    -- Use input_q in downstream logic; review any input_data bypass.
Illustrative Verilog / SystemVerilog:
    // Same-clock input; adds a cycle of latency.
    always @(posedge clk) input_q <= input_data;
    // Use input_q downstream; review raw input_data bypasses.

